// REJECTS: Unexpected token ';'. Valid alternatives: ['.']
//
// A propertyView's `property` is always `<ownerClassPath>.<propertyName>` -- the owning
// class is part of the reference, not inferred from the view's source classView.
//
// Inferring it is the obvious optimisation, and it is wrong: the source classView is a
// diagram-level name, the property reference is a model-level one, and a diagram may draw
// the same class twice. A rewrite that accepts a bare property name and resolves it
// against `source` produces a reference that is right in the common case and silently
// wrong whenever a class appears in two views.
###Diagram
Diagram fixture::neg::BareProperty
{
   propertyView
   {
      property: firm;
      source: a;
      target: b;
      points: [];
   }
}
